Rudolph

Santa doesn’t primarily need another factory.

He needs something that identifies where a small intervention can matter enormously.

Define the Rudolph Function:

R(i,g)=
\frac{
\mathbb E[
\text{downstream agency generated by giving }g\text{ to }i
]
}{
C(g)
